1. Recursive Hierarchy Traversal (01_recursive_hierarchy.sql)
Description: Utilizes a recursive common table expression (WITH RECURSIVE) to traverse organizational trees or parent-child hierarchical data. It starts from the root node (where manager_id is null) and iteratively steps down layer by layer, calculating the depth level for each employee.

Use Case: Organizational charts, bill-of-materials (BOM), category trees, and network routing.

2. Running Total Calculation (02_running_total.sql)
Description: Computes a cumulative sum across ordered rows using window functions (SUM() OVER (...)). By defining the frame clause as ROWS BETWEEN UNBOUNDED PRECEDING AND CURRENT ROW, it efficiently calculates running balances without complex self-joins or correlated subqueries.

Use Case: Financial ledgers, bank account balances, and cumulative metric tracking.

3. Weekly Moving Average (03_moving_average.sql)
Description: Employs windowed aggregation with a sliding row frame (ROWS BETWEEN 6 PRECEDING AND CURRENT ROW) to calculate a rolling average across a specific window of data points.

Use Case: Smoothing out high-frequency volatility in time-series data like daily sales, web traffic, or stock prices.

4. Pivot Aggregation (04_pivot_aggregation.sql)
Description: Converts row-level categorical date data into horizontal columns using conditional aggregation (SUM(CASE WHEN ... THEN ... END)). This transforms time-series transaction logs into clean, wide-format reports.

Use Case: Generating monthly or quarterly summary reports and financial matrices.

5. Gaps and Islands Analysis (05_gaps_and_islands.sql)
Description: Solves the classic "gaps and islands" problem by subtracting a sequence generated by ROW_NUMBER() from the actual date values. This groups contiguous blocks of dates into distinct "islands" so you can find continuous active periods.

Use Case: Identifying continuous user login streaks, server uptime periods, or subscription intervals.

6. Percentile Ranking (06_percentile_ranking.sql)
Description: Uses the PERCENT_RANK() window function partitioned by a category (e.g., department) to calculate the relative standing of a value within its partition on a scale from 0 to 1.

Use Case: Compensation benchmarking, performance reviews, and statistical grading.

7. Lead and Lag Delta Evaluation (07_lead_lag_delta.sql)
Description: Leverages the LAG() window function to look backward at the immediately preceding event timestamp within a user session partition, calculating the exact time delta between actions.

Use Case: Clickstream analytics, user behavior drop-off analysis, and manufacturing cycle time tracking.

8. JSON Array Aggregation (08_string_agg_json.sql)
Description: Groups records by a dimension and uses database-native functions (JSON_AGG and JSON_BUILD_OBJECT) to bundle child entities into structured JSON arrays directly within the SQL result set.

Use Case: Building nested API payloads, denormalizing relational data for NoSQL stores, and data serialization.

9. Conditional Rollup Aggregation (09_conditional_rollup.sql)
Description: Uses the ROLLUP operator in a GROUP BY clause to automatically generate multi-level subtotals and a grand total across multiple dimensions in a single efficient table scan.

Use Case: Executive summary dashboards and hierarchical financial reporting.

10. Self-Join Overlap Matching (10_self_join_match.sql)
Description: Performs an optimized self-join on a table containing time ranges (start_time and end_time) to identify conflicting schedules or overlapping intervals while preventing duplicate pairings.

Use Case: Room booking systems, resource scheduling, and calendar conflict detection.
